": \"Since the implementation of the congestion charge, traffic delays _________ by 22%.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"fell\",\n          \"falls\",\n          \"have fallen\",\n          \"were falling\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"have fallen\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Sentences beginning with \\\"Since + past event\\\" take present perfect (\\\"have fallen\\\") in the main clause.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g01-q08\",\n        \"prompt\": \"The pie charts indicate that in 2005, nuclear power _________ for 18% of domestic energy.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"accounts\",\n          \"has accounted\",\n          \"had been accounting\",\n          \"accounted\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"accounted\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Past simple (\\\"accounted\\\") must be used for the historical data point \\\"in 2005\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g01-q09\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Currently, renewable energy technologies _________ rapid global investment.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"are attracting\",\n          \"attracted\",\n          \"has attracted\",\n          \"were attracting\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"are attracting\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"Currently\\\" indicates a present ongoing process, making the present continuous (\\\"are attracting\\\") appropriate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g01-q10\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Prior to 2008, few corporations _________ telecommuting as a viable workplace alternative.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"considered\",\n          \"had considered\",\n          \"have considered\",\n          \"are considering\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"had considered\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Past perfect (\\\"had considered\\\") marks an action occurring prior to the past baseline year (2008).\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"gram-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Future Forms & Projections in IELTS Writing\",\n    \"focus\": \"Expressing demographic and economic projections up to 2030, 2050, or beyond.\",\n    \"explanation\": \"IELTS charts frequently extrapolate data into future years (e.g. 2030, 2050). Examiners penalize candidates who write \\\"will increase\\\" without qualifying it as a projection, because future data in charts represents an estimate, not a guaranteed historical certainty. Use phrases like \\\"is projected to rise\\\", \\\"is forecasted to surpass\\\", or future perfect \\\"will have doubled\\\".\",\n    \"bandTips\": \"Use passive hedging verbs: \\\"is predicted to\\\", \\\"is estimated to\\\", \\\"is expected to\\\", rather than bare \\\"will\\\".\",\n    \"exercises\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q01\",\n        \"prompt\": \"By 2040, the global human population _________ to reach approximately 9 billion.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"was projected\",\n          \"projected\",\n          \"is projected\",\n          \"is project\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is projected\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Passive structure \\\"is projected to reach\\\" accurately expresses future demographic modeling.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q02\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Solar power generation _________ to outstrip coal combustion by the end of this decade.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"expects\",\n          \"expected\",\n          \"was expecting\",\n          \"is expected\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is expected\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Use the passive \\\"is expected to outstrip\\\" because solar generation is the subject being predicted.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q03\",\n        \"prompt\": \"By the year 2050, researchers estimate that electric vehicle sales _________ fourfold.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"will have multiplied\",\n          \"will multiply\",\n          \"multiplied\",\n          \"are multiplying\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"will have multiplied\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Future perfect (\\\"will have multiplied\\\") expresses an action completed before a specified future deadline (\\\"By the year 2050\\\").\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q04\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Water consumption in urban sectors _________ forecasted to expand by 35%.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"are\",\n          \"is\",\n          \"was\",\n          \"were\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"Water consumption\\\" is an uncountable singular noun, so \\\"is forecasted\\\" is correct.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q05\",\n        \"prompt\": \"It is predicted _________ renewable sources will supply over 60% of total electrical demand by 2035.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"which\",\n          \"what\",\n          \"that\",\n          \"where\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"that\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The anticipatory \\\"It is predicted that + clause\\\" is the standard academic projection formula.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q06\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Global crude oil reserves are anticipated _________ significantly lower levels by 2060.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"reaching\",\n          \"reach\",\n          \"reached\",\n          \"to reach\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"to reach\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The verb \\\"anticipate\\\" in passive takes an infinitive with to: \\\"are anticipated to reach\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q07\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Over the subsequent twenty years, fertility rates _________ to plateau.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"are likely\",\n          \"is likely\",\n          \"likely\",\n          \"are likelihood\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"are likely\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"Fertility rates\\\" is plural, so \\\"are likely to plateau\\\" is grammatically correct.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q08\",\n        \"prompt\": \"According to government estimates, offshore wind capacity _________ by 2030.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"doubles\",\n          \"will have doubled\",\n          \"has doubled\",\n          \"was doubled\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"will have doubled\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"By 2030\\\" indicates completion by a future point, requiring future perfect (\\\"will have doubled\\\").\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q09\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Municipal authorities expect that the new subway line _________ completed by next October.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"is\",\n          \"was\",\n          \"will be\",\n          \"had been\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"will be\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Future passive \\\"will be completed\\\" accurately describes an upcoming infrastructure project.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g02-q10\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Petroleum usage is slated _________ steadily over the next two decades.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"declining\",\n          \"decline\",\n          \"declined\",\n          \"to decline\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"to decline\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"Be slated to + infinitive\\\" means scheduled or expected to happen.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"gram-03\",\n    \"title\": \"Conditionals in Task 2 Academic Arguments\",\n    \"focus\": \"Deploying First, Second, Third, and Mixed conditionals to construct persuasive hypothetical arguments.\",\n    \"explanation\": \"Conditionals allow you to evaluate potential outcomes, consequences, and historical alternatives in IELTS Task 2. First conditional (If + present, will + verb) evaluates real policy outcomes. Second conditional (If + past, would + verb) explores hypothetical policy reforms. Third conditional (If + past perfect, would have + past participle) reviews historical causes.\",\n    \"bandTips\": \"Use \\\"Unless\\\" (Unless governments act...) as a powerful alternative to \\\"If not\\\". Invert formal conditionals: \\\"Were governments to intervene...\\\" instead of \\\"If governments intervened...\\\".\",\n    \"exercises\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q01\",\n        \"prompt\": \"If municipal governments _________ in cycling infrastructure, fewer commuters would drive private cars.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"invested\",\n          \"invest\",\n          \"had invested\",\n          \"will invest\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"invested\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Second conditional (hypothetical present/future): \\\"If + past simple (invested), would + infinitive (would drive)\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q02\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Unless international bodies _________ carbon emissions promptly, climate degradation will accelerate.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"curbed\",\n          \"curb\",\n          \"will curb\",\n          \"would curb\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"curb\",\n        \"explanation\": \"First conditional with \\\"unless\\\" takes present simple (\\\"curb\\\") in the subordinate condition clause.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q03\",\n        \"prompt\": \"If public authorities had enacted smoking bans earlier, thousands of premature deaths _________ prevented.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"would be\",\n          \"will be\",\n          \"would have been\",\n          \"had been\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"would have been\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Third conditional (unreal past): \\\"If + past perfect (had enacted), would have been + past participle\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q04\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Were the government _________ higher taxes on sugary beverages, consumption would decline noticeably.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"levies\",\n          \"levied\",\n          \"will levy\",\n          \"to levy\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"to levy\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Formal inverted conditional: \\\"Were + subject + to-infinitive (Were the government to levy)\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q05\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Had health officials alerted the public sooner, the epidemic _________ so rapidly.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"would not have spread\",\n          \"would not spread\",\n          \"will not spread\",\n          \"had not spread\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"would not have spread\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Inverted third conditional: \\\"Had + subject + past participle, would not have + past participle\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q06\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Provided that schools _________ sufficient funding, creative arts programs can flourish.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"received\",\n          \"receive\",\n          \"will receive\",\n          \"had received\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"receive\",\n        \"explanation\": \"\\\"Provided that\\\" functions like \\\"if\\\" and takes present simple (\\\"receive\\\") when discussing real future conditions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q07\",\n        \"prompt\": \"If teenagers spend excessive hours on digital screens, their sleep quality _________ compromised.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"was\",\n          \"would be\",\n          \"is\",\n          \"were\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Zero conditional for scientific or factual cause-and-effect: present simple in both clauses.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q08\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Should tuition fees _________ further, many underprivileged students will be excluded from university.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"rose\",\n          \"risen\",\n          \"will rise\",\n          \"rise\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"rise\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Formal conditional inversion: \\\"Should + subject + bare infinitive (Should tuition fees rise)\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q09\",\n        \"prompt\": \"If remote work _________ universally available, housing demands in central metropolitan zones would drop.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"were\",\n          \"is\",\n          \"will be\",\n          \"has been\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"were\",\n        \"explanation\": \"In formal academic subjunctive second conditionals, \\\"were\\\" is preferred over \\\"was\\\" for all persons.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g03-q10\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Children will struggle to develop social empathy unless they _________ in face-to-face peer play.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"engaged\",\n          \"engage\",\n          \"will engage\",\n          \"would engage\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"engage\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Clause following \\\"unless\\\" takes present simple (\\\"engage\\\") in a real predictive conditional.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"gram-04\",\n    \"title\": \"The Passive Voice in Academic Writing & Processes\",\n    \"focus\": \"Using the passive voice to maintain objective scientific detachment and describe process steps.\",\n    \"explanation\": \"The passive voice is fundamental in IELTS Writing. In Task 1 process diagrams, the agent (who did it) is irrelevant; the object and the action matter (e.g., \\\"The water is heated\\\", \\\"The tea leaves are harvested and dried\\\"). In Task 2, the passive voice avoids informal personal pronouns like \\\"I think\\\" or \\\"People do\\\" by focusing on the action: \\\"It is often argued that...\\\", \\\"Stricter penalties should be enforced\\\".\",\n    \"bandTips\": \"When describing processes in Task 1, use present simple passive: [is/are + past participle].\",\n    \"exercises\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q01\",\n        \"prompt\": \"In the second stage of the recycling process, the plastic bottles _________ by color.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"sort\",\n          \"is sorted\",\n          \"are sorted\",\n          \"were sorted\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"are sorted\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Plural noun (\\\"bottles\\\") in a present general process diagram takes \\\"are sorted\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q02\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Subsequently, the crushed pulp _________ to a high temperature to remove moisture.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"heats\",\n          \"are heated\",\n          \"heated\",\n          \"is heated\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is heated\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Uncountable singular noun (\\\"pulp\\\") takes singular present passive: \\\"is heated\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q03\",\n        \"prompt\": \"It _________ that access to clean drinking water is a fundamental human entitlement.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"is widely acknowledged\",\n          \"widely acknowledges\",\n          \"was widely acknowledging\",\n          \"is widely acknowledge\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is widely acknowledged\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The impersonal passive \\\"It is widely acknowledged that...\\\" creates a formal, objective academic tone.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q04\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Once the tea leaves _________, they are transported to processing factories.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"have dried\",\n          \"are dried\",\n          \"dry\",\n          \"will be dried\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"are dried\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Present simple passive \\\"are dried\\\" matches the sequential process convention.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q05\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Stringent carbon taxes ought to _________ on heavy fossil fuel industries.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"impose\",\n          \"imposed\",\n          \"be imposed\",\n          \"been imposed\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"be imposed\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Modal passive structure: modal verb (\\\"ought to\\\") + be + past participle (\\\"be imposed\\\").\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q06\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Over twenty thousand survey questionnaires _________ by the university research team last year.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"analyzed\",\n          \"are analyzed\",\n          \"have been analyzed\",\n          \"were analyzed\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"were analyzed\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Past passive \\\"were analyzed\\\" matches the past timeframe indicator \\\"last year\\\".\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q07\",\n        \"prompt\": \"The filtered brine _________ into the cooling chamber through automated pipes.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"is pumped\",\n          \"pumps\",\n          \"are pumped\",\n          \"pumped\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"is pumped\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Singular noun (\\\"brine\\\") takes \\\"is pumped\\\" in process descriptions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q08\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Significant breakthroughs _________ in the treatment of cardiovascular disorders.\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"achieved\",\n          \"have been achieved\",\n          \"have achieved\",\n          \"were achieving\"\n        ],\n        \"correctAnswer\": \"have been achieved\",\n        \"explanation\": \"Present perfect passive: \\\"have been achieved\\\" indicates ongoing historical progress.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"g04-q09\",\n        \"prompt\": \"Underage offenders should _________ toward community restitution rather than